  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Steppin'** (1 review): Reviewer recommends sampling this opening track to hear how good the recording sounds [3]\n- **Jesus Children Of America** (1 review): Reviewer singles out the keyboard solo in this song as the show's highlight [4]\n- **So Live** (1 other source): So Live runs into the drum feature, which leads into One in Seven [1]\n- **Music Take Your Mind** (1 review): James Hurt sat in on keys and Zak Najor on drums for this song [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Drumz**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Music Take Your Mind**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Liquid [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2001-09-01.shnf** (recommended): source not stated; 8 songs; 116 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Recorded with mk21h mics; reviewer finds the recording excellent [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Private, family-style gathering in Wicker Park with a local crowd, part of the Chicago Festival of Funk and Groove [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2001-09-01.shnf**: taped by Kurt Ruthe & Mike Yurkus; transferred by Kurt Ruthe; source: Schoeps mk21h (On Stage, ORTF) > kc-5 > cmc6 > VMS52UB > AD2K+ > Sony PCM-M1 [1]. Also: Mics stood on stage, 3.5 feet from the B3 lip on the Neal side, ortf configuration [1]",
